{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Fund pelvic health education in schools, taught by specialist physiotherapists",
        "additional_details": "Why wait until someone develops a health problem before teaching them how their body works?\r\nPhysiotherapists already use muscular coordination and pelvic floor rehabilitation to treat back pain and bladder and bowel dysfunction. Yet children, particularly boys, rarely receive this education. \r\nSpecialist physiotherapists could teach these essential functions through PSHE, potentially improving lifelong health and reducing future NHS costs in particular nonspecific low back pain and constipation",
        "background": "We call for Funding of age-appropriate pelvic health education for boys and girls in primary and secondary schools, delivered directly by specialist pelvic health physiotherapists. Teach bladder, bowel and pelvic floor function, breathing and spinal control to support lifelong health as part of PSHE",
